  "important_caveat": "From June 2012 to May 2019 the ESA multi-sensor record is itself built from MODIS on Terra (ESA's own L3C V4.50 processing of Terra MODIS). So ESA is independent of the NASA MOD11C3 product and of Terra's late-record drift only in 2001-2011 (ATSR-2/AATSR) and 2019-2024 (Sentinel-3B); in 2012-2018 it shares the Terra instrument with C-A.",
  "time_of_day_handling": "The user guide says the multi-sensor record is intercalibrated to IASI and then given a temporal correction to a common local equatorial crossing time, with Terra MODIS as the reference sensor. It documents this for the v2.0 record; the v3.00 monthly files used here carry no time-correction variable, so how far the correction applies to these v3.00 daytime months is not confirmed from the files.",
  "known_breaks": "The guide names the sensor transitions (ATSR-2 to AATSR 2002, AATSR to Terra MODIS 2012, Terra MODIS to Sentinel-3 SLSTR) and warns that inconsistencies or discontinuities may occur when sensors change; its stability line for the ATSR-2/AATSR period is -0.41 to 0.25 K per decade (global, against air temperature). No step sizes are published for this region."
 },
